From: OpenWrt community
Subject: [PATCH] embest: mx6boards: enable the FEC clocks for the AR8035 PHY

The MarS Board and the RIoTboard use an AR8035 PHY connected via RGMII.
Two clock setups have to be in place before the fec driver can talk to
the PHY:

1. The ENET peripheral clock gate (CCM CCGR1). This U-Boot builds
   neither with SPL nor with CONFIG_CLK_CCF, so nothing ever enables
   it: the DCD only initializes the DDR and the fec driver handles
   its clocks only on the CCF/IMX8 code paths. With the gate closed
   the FEC registers (including the MDIO engine) are dead,
   phy_connect() fails during probe and U-Boot reports "No ethernet
   found" / "No MDIO bus found" even with the PHY reset line properly
   toggled. The vendor U-Boot does not show this problem because its
   lowlevel init sets all CCGR registers to 0xffffffff.

2. The ENET reference clock: enable the ANATOP ENET PLL and select it
   via IOMUXC GPR1[ENET_CLK_SEL], like board/solidrun/mx6cuboxi does
   for the same PHY family. (The PHY on these boards carries its own
   25 MHz crystal, so this mainly matches the known-good reference
   configuration the kernel uses.)

Do both from board_init(). RIoTboard benefits from this as well.

--- a/board/embest/mx6boards/mx6boards.c
+++ b/board/embest/mx6boards/mx6boards.c
@@ -114,6 +114,37 @@
 	dm_gpio_free(phy_rst.dev, &phy_rst);
 }
 
+static int setup_fec(void)
+{
+	struct iomuxc *const iomuxc_regs = (struct iomuxc *)IOMUXC_BASE_ADDR;
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Open the ENET peripheral clock gate. This is neither an SPL nor
+	 * a CONFIG_CLK_CCF build, so nothing else ever enables it: the DCD
+	 * only initializes the DDR and the fec driver handles its clocks
+	 * only on CCF/IMX8 builds. With the gate closed the FEC registers
+	 * (including the MDIO engine) are dead.
+	 */
+	enable_enet_clk(1);
+
+	/*
+	 * Enable the ANATOP ENET PLL and route it to the ENET reference
+	 * clock, like the kernel and board/solidrun/mx6cuboxi do for the
+	 * same PHY family. (The PHY on these boards carries its own
+	 * 25 MHz crystal, so this mainly matches the known-good
+	 * reference configuration.)
+	 */
+	ret = enable_fec_anatop_clock(0, ENET_25MHZ);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* set gpr1[ENET_CLK_SEL] */
+	setbits_le32(&iomuxc_regs->gpr[1], IOMUXC_GPR1_ENET_CLK_SEL_MASK);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 int mx6_rgmii_rework(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	/* from linux/arch/arm/mach-imx/mach-imx6q.c :
@@ -417,6 +448,7 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_MXC_SPI
 	setup_spi();
 #endif
+	setup_fec();
 	return 0;
 }
 
